        &lt;SUBSERVICE qualifier="DID_9F_Previous_Stored_Repair_Shop_Code_Or_Tester_Serial_Number" id="0x0f1de284" active="true" actQual="ReadDid"&gt;
          &lt;CFGVARIANTREFS&gt;
            &lt;CFGVARIANTREF ref="0x15406144"/&gt;
          &lt;/CFGVARIANTREFS&gt;
          &lt;DESC&gt;This DID contains the Previous Stored Repair Shop Code Or Tester Serial Numbers.  This data provides a mechanism for a tool user to identify up to the last two dealer codes or tester serial numbers programmed into DID $98.

Last Stored Repair Shop Code or Tester Serial Number
When a test tool writes a dealer code or tester serial number into DID $98, the data previously stored in DID $98 is copied (without additional tester intervention) into the module memory housing byte positions 0 through 9 of this DID.

Second from Last Stored Repair Shop Code or Tester Serial Number
When a test tool writes a dealer code or tester serial number into DID $98, the data previously in byte positions 0 through 9 of this DID are moved to positions 10 through 19.  The data previously stored in DID $98 are then copied into this DID in byte positions 0 through 9.&lt;/DESC&gt;
