          &lt;/PROTCOMPCOLPOOL&gt;
        &lt;/SUBSERVICE&gt;
        &lt;SUBSERVICE qualifier="DID_CC_Base_Model_Part_Number" id="0x0f1e69bc" active="true" actQual="ReadDid"&gt;
          &lt;CFGVARIANTREFS&gt;
            &lt;CFGVARIANTREF ref="0x15406144"/&gt;
          &lt;/CFGVARIANTREFS&gt;
          &lt;DESC&gt;As used by EPS, this number represents the End Model Part Number of the ECU only.
This DID is used to identify the part number that represents the unique combination of ECU hardware and all non-reprogrammable software (e.g. Boot software) which is used during SPS programming. The BMPN must be stored in the ECU in a non-erasable memory area (e.g. boot sector of flash, or EEPROM). It shall not be possible to change the BMPN as part of a programming session or through diagnostic services when a programming session is not active. The BMPN of a service replacement ECU shall be identical to that of a â€œProduction ECUâ€ if both ECUâ€™s have the same hardware and non-reprogrammable software.
If an Alpha Code is used, then the Alpha Code associated with this part number shall be stored in DID $DC.
* See Note 1 at the beginning of this section.&lt;/DESC&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="PacketHandlerSupport" value="None"/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="MainHandlerSupport" value="User"/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="PreHandlerSupport" value="None"/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="PreHandlerOverrideName" value=""/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="PostHandlerSupport" value="None"/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="PostHandlerOverrideName" value=""/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="NvmBlockDescriptor" value=""/&gt;
