          &lt;DESC&gt;Smooth Road Shake (SRS) measures the oscillation frequency of the road wheel and provides a â€œcounter-actionâ€ intended to compensate for the oscillation so it does not transfer to the steering wheel and thus, will not be felt by the driver.  This PID provides the amount of Smooth Road Shake (SRS)  compensation scaled to a calibrateable maximum allowable value.  0 indicates maximum allowable SRS compensation or greater and 100 indicates a minimal or no SRS compensation.&lt;/DESC&gt;
