          &lt;/CFGVARIANTREFS&gt;
          &lt;DESC&gt;This PID provides the State of Health of the controller based on the temperature of the controller. 100 indicates the temperature is normal (within calibratable range). 1 to 99 indicates controller temperature has passed a calibratable threshold.  0 indicates that the temperature has passed a minimum or maximum threshold allowed. The Out of Range byte is to notifiy which thresholds have been exceeded within the ignition cycle.&lt;/DESC&gt;
