          &lt;/PROTCOMPCOLPOOL&gt;
        &lt;/SUBSERVICE&gt;
        &lt;SUBSERVICE qualifier="DID_D0_Boot_Software_Part_Number_Alpha_Code" id="0x155f4714" active="true" actQual="ReadDid"&gt;
          &lt;CFGVARIANTREFS&gt;
            &lt;CFGVARIANTREF ref="0x155bd254"/&gt;
          &lt;/CFGVARIANTREFS&gt;
          &lt;DESC&gt;This DID contains a 2 character ASCII representation of the Alpha Code associated with the Boot Software Part Number (stored in DID $C0). The Alpha Code consists of a Design Level Suffix (DLS) and a Process Level Suffix (PLS).
Byte 1 (DLS)
This byte is contains an ASCII value that represents the major software release. This value shall initially be set to A and incremented as appropriate.
Byte 2 (PLS)
This byte is contains an ASCII value that represents the minor software revision. This value shall initially be set to A and incremented as appropriate.&lt;/DESC&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="PacketHandlerSupport" value="None"/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="MainHandlerSupport" value="User"/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="PreHandlerSupport" value="None"/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="PreHandlerOverrideName" value=""/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="PostHandlerSupport" value="None"/&gt;
          &lt;ATTRIBUTE name="PostHandlerOverrideName" value=""/&gt;
